.TH "NIAC" "1" "Sep 2026" "NIAC" "NIAC Manual"

.SH NAME
niac-sanitize - Sanitize SNMP walk files with NIAC branding


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac sanitize   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sanitize SNMP walk files by replacing real network data with consistent
NiAC-Go branded data. IP addresses are mapped deterministically so the
same input IP always produces the same output IP.

.PP
What is KEPT (not sensitive):
  • Serial numbers
  • MAC addresses
  • Hardware models
  • Interface counts/types
  • VLAN IDs

.PP
What is TRANSFORMED (deterministic):
  • IP addresses → 10.0.0.0/8 (NiAC-Go network)
  • Hostnames → niac---
  • DNS domains → niac-go.com / niac-go.local
  • Contact info → netadmin@niac-go.com
  • Location strings → NiAC-Go - DC-WEST
  • Community strings → public or niac-go-ro


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--batch\fP[=false]
	Batch process multiple files

.PP
\fB--check\fP[=false]
	Report walks that are not safe to ship instead of writing sanitized copies

.PP
\fB--community\fP="public"
	SNMP community string

.PP
\fB--contact\fP="netadmin@niac-go.com"
	Contact email

.PP
\fB--domain\fP="niac-go.com"
	Domain for hostnames and DNS

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for sanitize

.PP
\fB--input-dir\fP=""
	Input directory for batch mode

.PP
\fB--location\fP="DC-WEST"
	Default location suffix

.PP
\fB--mapping-file\fP=""
	JSON file to load/save IP mappings

.PP
\fB--output-dir\fP=""
	Output directory for batch mode


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Sanitize a single walk file
  niac sanitize device.walk device-sanitized.walk

  # Batch mode - sanitize all walks in a directory
  niac sanitize --batch --input-dir walks/ --output-dir sanitized/

  # Use persistent mapping file
  niac sanitize --mapping-file ip-map.json device.walk output.walk

  # Check walks are safe to ship (exit 1 when any is not)
  niac sanitize --check internal/library/starter/walks/*.walk
.EE


